  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the brief, memory guidance, and current source, then extend the existing store and handlers. I\u2019ll verify migration and concurrency behavior with the supplied tests and local cross-process requests.",
    "The brief defines version 1, and the follow-up changes that contract to version 2. I\u2019m applying the follow-up to the existing transaction path so replay, claims, and fencing retain their current behavior. I\u2019m also reading the installed OpenSocrates and checkpoint guidance for this enrolled task.",
    "I found one expected mismatch in the preserved tests: an earlier test assumes a newly submitted job is immediately eligible after lease expiry, while the follow-up sets a 1,000 ms retry default. I\u2019ll keep that test unchanged, implement the new contract, and report its result alongside focused follow-up checks.",
    "The first test run compiles and reaches the preserved lifecycle test. It fails at the expected lease-expiry assertion because the new retry delay keeps that job unavailable at the old deadline. I\u2019ll add focused tests for the new timing, capacity, pagination, and migration behavior, then run race tests and process-level checks.",
    "Focused scheduling, cancellation, pagination, and two-store admission tests now pass. I\u2019m moving to a version 1 database created by the prior source, then checking live leases and idempotency replay through migration. After that I\u2019ll run the server from two processes against one file.",
    "A version 1 database from the prior source migrated while two new server processes started. Its original submission replayed with the same job ID, a changed command conflicted, and the live lease could be heartbeated and completed across processes. Separate cross-process requests passed pending and inflight checks; an unknown future schema also failed startup without changing the database file hash.",
    "The new and unaffected earlier queue tests pass under the race detector. The full race suite still stops at the preserved lifecycle assertion that expects immediate retry. I\u2019m checking one more migration edge: a historical version 1 job must keep its zero retry base after its lease expires.",
    "The historical lease check passed: the migrated job was reclaimable at its expired deadline and retained `retry_base_ms: 0`. I tightened validation for explicit `null` input fields and malformed cursors, then reran the focused tests. I\u2019m doing the final full-suite check and removing the temporary legacy binaries and databases.",
    "The final full race command still fails only at the preserved immediate-retry assertion; focused race tests, build, vet, and diff checks pass. I\u2019m checking simultaneous migration startup once more, since the earlier process probe started the two new servers one after the other.",
    "Implemented the QueueForge version 2 follow-up in the disposable workspace. The existing [submission, claim, and lease paths](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/store.go:238) now handle scheduling and admission; the same store adds [transactional migration](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/store.go:84), cancellation, and bounded keyset listing. [HTTP validation and routes](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/http.go:96), [CLI limits](<WORKSPACE>/cmd/server/main.go:24), tests, and README are updated.\n\nThe new indexes support priority claims, live lease counts, and tenant or queue pagination by creation sequence. Migration leaves historical retry bases at zero and preserves legacy idempotency fingerprints.\n\n**Verification:** focused queue tests passed with `-race`; build, vet, driver tests, and `git diff --check` passed. Loopback probes passed for simultaneous two-process migration, legacy replay and live-lease continuity, historical expiry timing, cross-process limits, and future-schema file-byte invariance. Owned probe processes were stopped.\n\n**Remaining test conflict:** `go test -race ./...` fails at the preserved `TestLifecycleAndIsolation` assertion on line 94. It expects immediate reclaim of a newly submitted job at lease expiry; version 2 requires that job\u2019s default 1,000 ms retry delay. The supplied test was left unchanged."
  ],
